From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blong <belohnung@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:04:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Rejoin the SFU after it drops us

When the SFU restarts or loses the room, livekit-client's resume gets a 404
and gives up, and nothing reconnected afterwards. The local Connection now
watches for an unexpected Disconnected, fetches a fresh JWT (which makes the
JWT service recreate the room) and reconnects with backoff for about a minute
before surfacing an error. The Publisher republishes mic and camera once the
room is rejoined, as LiveKit stops local tracks on disconnect.

Ported to v0.24.0 from largelanguagemeowing/cinny e3953586 (with its
formatting follow-up 7b00e18a). doOpenIdAndJWTFromUrl gained a logger
parameter upstream; the rest applied by context.

Rebased onto v0.26.1: upstream dropped JwtEndpointVersion and the
delayed-leave parameters from the JWT request (5cfe7ea4, cff8766a), so
the refresh closure now passes { matrixRTCMode } and ConnectionOpts no
longer carries forceJwtEndpoint. Upstream still has no rejoin after a
final Disconnected.

Rebased onto v0.28.1: the LiveKit code moved into the SDK
(sdk/src/media-backend/livekit) and Connection now fetches its own token
through getSFUConfig() (24b6a632), so the refreshSFUConfig closure through
LocalTransport, ConnectionFactory and ConnectionManager is gone: the rejoin
calls getSFUConfig() again, which for a ResolvedConnection also publishes the
fresh token on resolved$. The error state is { state: "error", error } with
the SDK's FailToStartLivekitConnection. Publisher is now driven by LocalMedia's
desired map, so the republish restarts it (start() again) instead of reading
mute states; its test rooms gained an event emitter. Upstream still has no
rejoin after a final Disconnected.
